  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (0.00) and model shows persistent overestimation.",
    "Correct for lagged underestimation in early periods (e.g., 1–3 days after spike) by adding 0.5–1.0 to forecast if sentiment remains flat.",
    "Avoid overshoot after sharp price spikes — reduce forecast by 10–15% if sentiment is 0.00 and price rises >5% from prior day.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast deviates >2.0 from 30-day moving average, adjust toward average by 0.3–0.7 per day.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment when >0.5 — model should respond to bullish sentiment with 0.5–1.0% upward adjustment per day."
  ]
}
